AUTOTOP: ARK1668 audio as stock 3.4 runs it on the BM168.

- I2S blocks: the control values stock leaves in them (devmem, constant
  while idle, recording and playing), including the DMA request enables the
  SDK left commented out; stock's clock-generator step/modulo pairs; mic
  front-end gain and enhance as module parameters (stock: 0, off).
- PCM: ark-dma.c has no dmaengine cyclic callback, so the generic
  dmaengine PCM failed every start with -ENOMEM (SPIKE14). Use its
  dw_dma_cyclic_* API directly, as stock's snd-soc-ark-pcm-dma does, with
  the position read from the channel's memory-side address register.
  Downstream de1e2ad does the same but mirrors the private descriptor with a
  layout that differs from this SDK's; include the real header instead.
- SDDAC: stock's control names (numid 1/2), working volume, and mute that
  clears the volume register as stock's ark_audio_mute does (downstream
  fd81d03/f419add reviewed, not taken as is).
- BD37033: fix the build (void function returning a value, as downstream)
  and a double free on remove (devm memory passed to kfree).

